Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:37:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/31] Add the Doc package with its model and dmc clients

doc/ is a separate Dart package (dmc_doc, executable doc). dmc itself
stays free of models; the root analyzer excludes doc/.

- One OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions client (POST
  {baseUrl}/chat/completions, GET {baseUrl}/models). It retries 429 and
  5xx with exponential backoff and jitter (honouring Retry-After up to
  30 s), has clear connect and response timeouts, keeps only
  message.content (reasoning_content is dropped), and never puts the
  API key in an error or log.
- Provider rules: meta always sends reasoning_effort (default low,
  never none) and max_completion_tokens, and never stop, n, logit_bias,
  penalties, max_tokens or a temperature. baseten and local send
  max_tokens.
- Config in the user config dir (dmc-doc/config.json): providers
  (meta https://api.meta.ai/v1 with MODEL_API_KEY, baseten
  https://inference.baseten.co/v1 with BASETEN_API_KEY, local Ollama at
  127.0.0.1:11434 with no key), published per-model prices, budgets
  (meta $150, baseten $100), and role routing. usage.json records
  tokens and cost per provider.
- A dmc client that finds dmc via --dmc, DMC_BIN, then PATH, checks it
  with capabilities --json --schema-version 1, skips Apple's
  /usr/bin/dmc without running it and older dmc builds, and runs
  commands with --json --schema-version 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
